# Fortress P0 security fixes
#
# Apply with:   git apply docs/p0-fixes.patch
# Review with:  git apply --check docs/p0-fixes.patch
#
# Covers:
#   H1 — API-key scopes are stored but never enforced.
#   H2 — Built-in /auth/impersonate has no permission gate.
#   H3 — Refresh-token rotation is not atomic (core + OAuth).
#
# Each hunk is independent; you can split with `git apply --include=` if you
# want to land them separately. Tests + CHANGELOG hunks live at the end.

---

## H2 — Gate the impersonation endpoint

The endpoint already declares `.security('bearer')` (any authenticated user).
The route's own description and the service-method JSDoc say the caller must
hold `fortress:impersonate`, but nothing in the public surface enforces it.

Two-line change at the route, plus a defense-in-depth check at the service
boundary so direct in-process callers (cron jobs, scripts) are also gated.

```diff
--- a/src/core/auth/auth-endpoints.ts
+++ b/src/core/auth/auth-endpoints.ts
@@
   impersonate: endpoint('POST', '/auth/impersonate')
     .summary('Impersonate a user')
     .description('Issue a short-lived, non-renewable token to act as another user. Requires fortress:impersonate permission.')
     .tags('Auth')
     .security('bearer')
+    .permission('fortress', 'impersonate')
     .body(obj(
