## H3 — Atomic refresh-token rotation (core)

The current sequence is `findRefreshTokenByHash → if isRevoked throw reuse →
update by id → create`. Two concurrent refreshes both read `isRevoked=false`
and both succeed, producing two valid descendants in the same family and
silently bypassing replay detection.

Fix: replace the find+update pair with a single conditional update that
atomically flips `isRevoked: false → true` and returns the row only to the
winner. Losers fall through into the reuse branch.

`DatabaseAdapter.update` already returns `T | null` (see `src/drizzle/adapter.ts:215-220`,
which uses `.returning()`), so no new adapter primitive is required.

